1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:00,920
Speaker 1: Good morning.

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:02,960
Speaker 1: Three things today.

3
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:08,340
Speaker 1: The lab phase two, the enforces agreement and the elective rollout.

4
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:11,080
Speaker 1: Pavan, start with the lab.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,380
Speaker 3: Ma'am, phase one is complete.

6
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:18,580
Speaker 3: Two workstations delivered on the 14th, installed and running.

7
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:23,060
Speaker 3: Total spend was 2.2 lakhs, exactly the approved figure.

8
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,500
Speaker 1: Any issues with installation?

9
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:28,480
Speaker 3: One.

10
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,420
Speaker 3: The lab's existing power circuit could not handle both machines at full load.

11
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,200
Speaker 3: We had to add a dedicated line.

12
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,760
Speaker 3: That cost 18,000 rupees, which I paid from the maintenance head.

13
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,440
Speaker 0: Was that approved?

14
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,180
Speaker 3: I informed the chairperson before spending.

15
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,320
Speaker 3: It was an emergency.

16
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:52,400
Speaker 1: I approved it verbally.

17
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:55,040
Speaker 1: Pawan, put it in writing.

18
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:56,640
Speaker 1: so the audit trail is clean.

19
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,920
Speaker 1: Now, phase 2.

20
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,260
Speaker 3: Good news here.

21
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,080
Speaker 3: GPU prices have come down.

22
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:10,060
Speaker 3: The same machine that quoted 1.12 locks in December is now 95,000.

23
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:12,600
Speaker 3: Two machines come to 1.9 locks.

24
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:17,740
Speaker 2: That's below what we budgeted for phase 2.

25
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:18,860
Speaker 3: Yes ma'am.

26
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:21,720
Speaker 3: We had planned 2.2 locks again.

27
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:24,340
Speaker 3: So we are 30,000 under.

28
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,760
Speaker 1: Then let's use the difference.

29
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:33,360
Speaker 1: Meera, you mentioned needing API credits for the language model module.

30
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:35,360
Speaker 2: I did.

31
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:41,020
Speaker 2: The new NLP syllabus has students fine-tuning and calling hosted models.

32
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:45,980
Speaker 2: 40,000 rupees would cover a full semester for 60 students.

33
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,260
Speaker 1: We have 30,000 spare.

34
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,580
Speaker 1: Can you manage with that?

35
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,420
Speaker 2: If students share team accounts, yes.

36
00:01:56,620 --> 00:02:00,100
Speaker 2: I'll restructure the assignment to be team-based rather than individual.

37
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:02,320
Speaker 1: Do that!

38
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:03,700
Speaker 1: Bhavan?

39
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:07,460
Speaker 1: Raise the phase to purchase order for 1.9 lakhs.

40
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:10,120
Speaker 1: What's the delivery timeline?

41
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:13,940
Speaker 3: Vendor says 3 weeks from purchase order.

42
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:18,280
Speaker 3: If I raise it this week, machines arrive by March 15.

43
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:21,720
Speaker 1: March 15 is the deadline then.

44
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:26,220
Speaker 1: The elective starts in April, so that gives us buffer.

45
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:28,900
Speaker 1: Ramesh, the syllabus.

46
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:35,480
Speaker 0: The board approved the applied deep learning syllabus with the revised assessment.

47
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:43,040
Speaker 0: 30% mini project, 30% continuous evaluation, 40% end semester.

48
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:47,640
Speaker 0: The mini project is the production deployment task we discussed.

49
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:49,520
Speaker 1: Good.

50
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,280
Speaker 1: Enrollment?

51
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:54,900
Speaker 0: 47 students registered.

52
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,600
Speaker 0: We capped it at 50.

53
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:00,720
Speaker 2: That's strong for a first offering.

54
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:03,820
Speaker 0: There's one complication.

55
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:09,180
Speaker 0: Of those 47, 19 have not taken machine learning.

56
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:15,580
Speaker 0: The board made ML a prerequisite, but that applies to next year's batch only.

57
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:19,300
Speaker 1: So this batch is grandfathered in.

58
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:21,260
Speaker 0: Correct.

59
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:27,700
Speaker 0: But 19 students without ML background in a deep learning course is a real problem.

60
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:30,700
Speaker 0: I'd like to run a bridge module.

61
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:33,520
Speaker 1: What would that involve?

62
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:38,200
Speaker 0: Four extra sessions before the semester starts.

63
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:43,540
Speaker 0: Linear algebra refresher Gradient descent, basic classification.

64
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:46,560
Speaker 0: Voluntary but strongly recommended.

65
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:48,860
Speaker 2: Who teaches it?

66
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:51,740
Speaker 0: I'll take two sessions.

67
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:55,120
Speaker 0: I was hoping Meera takes the other two.

68
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:57,520
Speaker 2: I can do that.

69
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:00,560
Speaker 2: Schedule them in the last week of March.

70
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:02,840
Speaker 1: Approved.

71
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,080
Speaker 1: Ramesh, you own the bridge module.

72
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:08,960
Speaker 1: Now the Infosys collaboration.

73
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:13,500
Speaker 1: The board prioritized it first among the three proposals.

74
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:18,899
Speaker 0: I spoke to their university relations head last Thursday.

75
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:24,180
Speaker 0: They want a joint research lab focused on applied machine learning.

76
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:30,740
Speaker 0: Their contribution is to engineers on site one day a week plus compute credits.

77
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,780
Speaker 1: And what do they want from us?

78
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:39,960
Speaker 0: Space and to faculty members committed at least six hours a week.

79
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:44,640
Speaker 0: They also want first look at student projects for hiring.

80
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:48,020
Speaker 2: First look at hiring is fine.

81
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:51,600
Speaker 2: First rights on intellectual property would not be.

82
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:56,040
Speaker 0: They have not asked for intellectual property.

83
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:58,480
Speaker 0: I raised it specifically.

84
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:01,320
Speaker 0: The draft says jointly owned.

85
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:04,760
Speaker 1: Jointly owned is acceptable.

86
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:08,940
Speaker 1: Who drafts the memorandum of understanding from our side?

87
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:11,780
Speaker 0: Legal will draft it.

88
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:13,620
Speaker 0: I'll coordinate.

89
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:19,000
Speaker 0: They want it signed before the board meets on February 28th.

90
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,320
Speaker 1: That's tight.

91
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:28,900
Speaker 1: Ramesh, target March 10 for the draft, and if it slips we present the status rather than the signature.

92
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,340
Speaker 1: Do not rush legal review to hit a date.

93
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:34,460
Speaker 0: Understood.

94
00:05:36,260 --> 00:05:37,660
Speaker 1: Pavan, one more thing.

95
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:43,120
Speaker 1: The capstone peer review is week 12 this year, not week 14.

96
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:46,560
Speaker 1: The board changed phase 1 to 14 weeks.

97
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,980
Speaker 1: Make sure the lab is bookable that week.

98
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:54,120
Speaker 3: I'll block the lab for the whole of week 12.

99
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:57,460
Speaker 2: On Capstone, I have a concern.

100
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:03,960
Speaker 2: Phase 1 is now 14 weeks, but the literature survey requirement is still 4 papers minimum.

101
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:07,600
Speaker 2: Students have more time and the same requirement.

102
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:10,340
Speaker 1: What do you propose?

103
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,160
Speaker 2: Raise it to 6 papers, or add a comparison matrix.

104
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:18,580
Speaker 2: Something that uses the extra 2 weeks.

105
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:23,020
Speaker 0: 6 papers is a lot for undergraduates.

106
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:26,120
Speaker 2: Then the comparison matrix.

107
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:31,780
Speaker 2: Same four papers, but they must compare methods across them on common criteria.

108
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:34,380
Speaker 1: I prefer that.

109
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,440
Speaker 1: Meera, write it into the rubric and send it to Priya.

110
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:41,680
Speaker 1: She is reviewing the rubric for fairness.

111
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:44,540
Speaker 2: I'll send it by Friday.

112
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:47,040
Speaker 1: Last item.

113
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:50,800
Speaker 1: The TCS placement drive results came in.

114
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:54,720
Speaker 1: 31 students placed out of 80 who sat.

115
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:59,360
Speaker 1: That's a better conversion than last year's 22.

116
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:02,120
Speaker 0: Any feedback from their panel?

117
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,320
Speaker 1: Yes, and it's useful.

118
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:10,400
Speaker 1: They said our students are strong on theory and weak on system design.

119
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:16,320
Speaker 1: Ramesh, that's worth feeding into the curriculum discussion at the next board meeting.

120
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:19,180
Speaker 0: I'll prepare a note.

121
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:21,060
Speaker 1: Good.

122
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:24,220
Speaker 1: Next meeting same time next week.

123
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:27,260
Speaker 1: Thank you.

